# One baseline for the two things that live side by side here:
#
#   site/     the Hugo site - the source of truth (content, config, layouts, assets, static,
#             the vendored hugo-theme-stack)
#   editor/   the editor app that reads, writes and builds that site
#
# The rule is "ignore what can be regenerated, what belongs to this machine, or what a tool
# produces at runtime". Everything a person wrote or configured is tracked - including the
# vendored theme (there is no Hugo Modules or submodule setup here, so the build needs those
# files to exist) and the 5.7 MB of fonts under site/static/, which the site really serves.
#
# Every pattern sits alone on its own line on purpose: gitignore has no trailing comments, so a
# line reading "site/public/  # output" would silently match nothing.

# --- the Hugo binary the editor shells out to ---
# 62 MB, downloaded rather than built here, and documented in editor/docs/site-elements.md.
.bin/

# --- state Hugo generates for the site ---
# published output: written only after a successful build, never hand-edited
site/public/
# Hugo's _gen cache (resized images, compiled assets), rebuilt on demand
site/resources/
# the lock file Hugo holds while a build is running, created on the first build; unanchored so it
# is ignored wherever Hugo puts it
.hugo_build.lock

# --- the editor's runtime state ---
# editor/.gitignore states the same four rules next to the code that owns them; they are repeated
# here so that ignoring works from the repository root even if that file is ever reorganised.
# npm install (matches at any depth)
node_modules/
# the built front end (npm run build:web); the server serves this directory
editor/dist/
# pre-save copies of source files, written by SafeWriter
editor/.backups/
# Hugo staging output and build cache, deliberately outside site/
editor/.build/

# --- local environment noise, never part of the project ---
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.log
*.swp
*~

# --- editor generated output ---
editor/public/
